language Essence 1.3

$ A sequence is a partial function, so applying it outside 1..|x| is undefined and the constraint
$ it sits in is false there. y = 3 is therefore not a solution, even though x's values leave
$ x(y) = 1 nothing to decide.
find x : sequence (size 2) of int(1)
find y : int(1..3)
such that x(y) = 1
